      "Ischemic cerebrovascular event (e.g., transient ischemic attack with amaurosis fugax) – rationale: unilateral left-arm numbness/weakness and transient left-eye vision disturbance raise concern for vascular source with cerebral or retinal ischemia; boxing-related neck strain could contribute; however, event duration and progression over weeks are atypical for a classic TIA"
    ],
    "I": [
      "Autoimmune/inflammatory demyelinating disease (e.g., MS presenting with optic neuritis and spinal/neuraxial sensory symptoms) – rationale: episode of transient left-eye vision change plus unilateral arm numbness/weakness and family autoimmune history; MS can present with optic symptoms and sensory deficits in different sites over time"
    ],
    "N": [
      "Neoplasm (e.g., brain/spinal cord lesion) – rationale: new focal neurological symptoms; though less likely given subacute, fluctuating course rather than a progressive mass effect, it remains possible without imaging"
    ],
    "D": [
      "Cervical spondylotic myelopathy / cervical radiculopathy – rationale: neck pain with left-arm numbness and weakness; could reflect nerve root or spinal cord involvement related to degenerative changes; boxing could precipitate or worsen"
    ],
    "I2": [
      "Iatrogenic/intoxication – rationale: recent heavy alcohol use and NSAID use could contribute to non-specific symptoms, but unlikely to explain focal unilateral arm numbness and transient monocular vision loss"
    ],
    "C": [
      "Congenital neuropathies or anatomical variations – rationale: less likely given acute/subacute presentation, but could contribute to nerve distribution symptoms if present"
    ],
    "A": [
      "Autoimmune/Allergic processes other than MS (e.g., other inflammatory neuropathies) – rationale: autoimmune milieu in family could predispose to CNS/PN inflammatory processes"
    ],
    "T": [
      "Traumatic injury to neck/shoulder or brachial plexus from boxing – rationale: boxing activity is ongoing and could cause local trauma contributing to arm numbness; however would not fully explain transient vision loss"
    ],
    "E": [
      "Endocrine/Metabolic neuropathies (e.g., B12 deficiency, diabetes, hypothyroidism) – rationale: family history of endocrine/aut autoimmune disease; could contribute to neuropathic symptoms, though focal presentation is less typical"
    ]
  },
